16 0 obj
<< /A 58 0 R /Alt (Flowchart displaying life course phases related to female health, detailing childhood to senior adulthood. Each phase associates with factors like cycle regularity, infertility, and cancer. Lifestyle influences, including nutrition and stress across all phases.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 59 0 R /Alt (Bar graph showing self-evaluated health by PCOS status across five categories: much better, slightly better, about the same, slightly worse, and much worse. Categories are divided by colors: red for PCOS, blue for possible PCOS, and green for no PCOS. The percentages vary across categories, with most respondents rating their health about the same.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 60 0 R /Alt (Three bar graphs analyzing menarche age and time to regularity by PCOS status. Chart A shows mean age at menarche; PCOS has a slightly lower mean than others. Chart B depicts percentages of menarche categories, with PCOS showing higher early menarche rates. Chart C compares the time taken for menstrual cycle regularity, indicating that \215No PCOS\216 has faster regularity achievement compared to PCOS and Possible PCOS groups.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 61 0 R /Alt (Bar charts displaying the relationship between PCOS status and various pregnancy variables. Chart A shows gravidity categories, with higher gravidity in 'No PCOS' group. Chart B indicates a higher percentage of infertility diagnoses in the 'PCOS' group. Chart C shows conception methods, with more IVF and artificial insemination in the 'PCOS' group, while natural conception is highest in 'No PCOS'. Chart D highlights complications during the first pregnancy, with 'PCOS' associated with more complications including any pregnancy complication and preeclampsia. Percentages and confidence intervals are provided.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 62 0 R /Alt (Bar charts showing the percentage of cardiometabolic conditions among different PCOS status groups: PCOS \(red\), Possible PCOS \(blue\), and No PCOS \(green\). Conditions include arrhythmia, coronary artery disease, heart attack, stroke, transient ischemic attack, congestive heart failure, and any metabolic condition. PCOS status is associated with higher percentages in each category. Arrhythmia is highest in the PCOS group at 6 percent, while any metabolic condition is 45.8 percent for PCOS, 29.2 for Possible PCOS, and 25.1 for No PCOS. Other conditions show smaller differences across groups.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 63 0 R /Alt (Bar chart showing percentages of endometrial hyperplasia and cancer among different PCOS statuses: PCOS, possible PCOS, and no PCOS. The hyperplasia panel shows PCOS at 1.6%, possible PCOS at 1.0%, and no PCOS at 0.4%. The cancer panel shows PCOS at 0.5%, possible PCOS at 0.3%, and no PCOS at 0.2%. Error bars indicate variability.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 46 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 64 0 R /Alt (Panel A depicts bar charts showing the percentage of self-reported mental health conditions by PCOS status: ADHD, Anorexia, Anxiety, Bipolar disorder, Bulimia, Depression, and Panic disorder. Panel B presents a graph of the mean PSS-4 score with confidence intervals across PCOS statuses, while Panel C displays percentages of PSS-4 scores above the median. Colors indicate PCOS \(red\), Possible PCOS \(blue\), and No PCOS \(green\).) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 47 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 65 0 R /Alt (Five side-by-side plots show mean BMI with 95% confidence intervals at ages eighteen, twenty-five, thirty-five, forty-five, and fifty-five. Each plot compares BMI across three groups: PCOS, Possible PCOS, and No PCOS. BMI increases with age in all groups, with PCOS consistently higher. The number of participants decreases with age.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 47 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 66 0 R /Alt (Chart A illustrates the percentages of individuals with different PCOS statuses following various diet types, showing a significant rise for no special diet. Chart B presents the frequency of fruit and vegetable intake by PCOS status, with a notable proportion consuming 4-7 times per week.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 48 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 67 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a line graph comparing physical activity levels among three groups: PCOS, Possible PCOS, and No PCOS. Activity levels range from no activity to strenuous. Panel B presents a stacked bar chart illustrating weekly exercise minutes across the same groups, categorized into five exercise duration ranges: 0 minutes, 1 to 75 minutes, 76 to 150 minutes, 151 to 300 minutes, and over 300 minutes per week.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 48 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
26 0 obj
<< /A 68 0 R /Alt (Four bar charts labeled A to D showing percentages of substance use by PCOS status.   A: Tobacco smoking status with categories of never, past, and current smoker.   B: Marijuana use frequency with categories of not at all, some days, and every day.   C: E-cigarette use frequency with the same categories as marijuana use.   D: Alcohol use status with categories of no or light, light or rare binge drinker, and moderate-to-heavy or frequent binge drinker.   Each chart compares PCOS, possible PCOS, and no PCOS groups.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 49 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
27 0 obj
<< /A 69 0 R /Alt (A three-panel figure illustrates sleep patterns and apnea diagnosis related to PCOS status. Panel A shows sleep hours per night, comparing weekdays and weekends. Most individuals, regardless of PCOS status, report 7 to 9 hours of sleep, with slightly fewer hours on weekdays. Panel B displays a bar graph of self-reported sleep apnea diagnosis percentages, highest for PCOS \(14.7%\), followed by Possible PCOS \(9.6%\), and No PCOS \(6.6%\). Panel C shows a stacked bar graph of the frequency of snort, gasp, or stop breathing, with most individuals reporting \215occasionally\216 or \215never,\216 across all PCOS statuses.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 50 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
